    "content": "<div class=\"article-content\">\n  <h2>Introduction: Desperation in the Red Ocean</h2>\n  <p>\"Polishing Wheel\" is a typical industrial commodity category. Giants abound (like 3M), price wars are brutal, and new products have almost no survival space.</p>\n  <p>Our user, Seller A, was about to give up on this category. But in one final attempt, he used FlowAI Agent to conduct a full scan of the Listings and Q&A sections of the Top 50 competitors.</p>\n\n  <h2>1. The \"Knowledge Gap\" AI Discovered</h2>\n  <p>FlowAgent discovered a high-frequency pattern when analyzing the \"User Questions\" section:</p>\n  <blockquote>\n    \"Can this handle aluminum rims?\"<br>\n    \"What compound should I use for stainless steel?\"<br>\n    \"Is this too harsh for chrome?\"\n  </blockquote>\n  <p><strong>Insight:</strong> Users don't lack \"wheels\"—they lack <strong>\"solutions tailored to specific materials.\"</strong> Current Listings all boast durability, but no one teaches users how to choose or how to use them.</p>\n\n  <h2>2. Strategy: Become an \"Expert\" Seller</h2>\n  <p>Based on AI recommendations, Seller A made changes:</p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Product Side:</strong> Instead of selling wheels individually, launch \"Aluminum Alloy Special Kit\" and \"Stainless Steel Mirror Kit\" bundled with matching polishing compounds.</li>\n    <li><strong>Content Side (Visual):</strong> Create a \"Material Comparison Chart\" image clearly listing which wheel suits which material and what RPM.</li>\n    <li><strong>Traffic Side (Keywords):</strong> Abandon the broad keyword \"Polishing Wheel\" and focus on scenario long-tail keywords like \"Aluminum Project Polishing Kit.\"</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>3. Results: High-Margin Blue Ocean</h2>\n  <p>While sales volume can't compete with 3M, Seller A's kit is priced at 3x competitor single products, with profit margins reaching 40%. He successfully avoided low-price competition and built his own <strong>\"professional moat.\"</strong></p>\n  <p>In commoditized competition, the <strong>\"information gap\"</strong> is the biggest blue ocean. And AI is the fastest shovel for obtaining that information gap.</p>\n</div>"
